; Feeds' transducer part: a feed's JSON events from its grammar's rule
; passes, for a host that reads parser events (dmog's `translate` and
; `run --grammar feed`). This is a library of definitions, each named
; `feed-transduce-...`, which a host links with its own program; its entry
; point is `feed-transduce`, and nothing else here is the host's to call.
;
; The tree is the one the reader builds by default, the Atom-shaped feed
; of an Atom 1.0 or 0.3 document and of an RSS 0.90 to 2.0 one, and every
; event is the one the walk of the reader's value gives, members in the
; reader's order: `format` and `version`, the feed's other members, and
; `entries` last. The reader converts the element tree only when the root
; element closes, so this part does what its conversion does, as the
; passes come. The feed's grammar is xml's with no rules of its own, so
; the passes are xml's: an `element`'s open carries its start tag's token,
; whose value is the element's name and its attributes in source order
; (an attribute the DOCTYPE defaults among them), a `child`'s open carries
; a text's token (a CDATA section's too, and an entity as its replacement
; text), and an `element`'s close ends it; the rest pass by.
;
; The reader reads an element of the feed's own level by its local name,
; the first of a name for a member of one value and every one for a list
; (authors, links, entries), and an element's text as its own text
; children joined and trimmed as JavaScript trims. So the part reads in
; two stages, with a router between them:
;
; - The reading (`feed-transduce-read`) writes, for each element of the
;   feed's own level the reader reads, a unit of a document of its own:
;   `start`, the dialect, at the root's start; `m` for a member of the
;   feed; `e` for an entry; and `ch` where an RSS feed's first channel
;   begins. A unit is the element's summary: its local name `l`, its
;   attributes `a`, and `c`, its texts and its elements' summaries, as deep
;   as the reader reads them (an entry's person's name), or, for an Atom
;   text construct or content of type xhtml, `x`, the pieces of the markup
;   the reader serialises, the inner markup of its first div between two
;   marks. Nothing is held: each event is written as its pass comes.
; - The router captures each unit as it ends: a member under
;   max_metadata_bytes, an entry on its own under max_record_bytes.
; - The writing (`feed-transduce-write`) writes `format` and `version` at
;   once. The reader computes each of the feed's other members from the
;   elements of the feed's whole level and writes them in an order of its
;   own, so the writing holds them until the first entry begins or the
;   feed ends, then writes them as the reader computes them, and then
;   each entry as its element closes.
;
; RSS allows a member of the feed after its first item, and Atom an
; element of the feed after its first entry. The reader reads them, but
; the feed's members are written by then: a member after the first entry
; that changes them is refused in the part's own words (`fail
; :unstreamable`, STREAMABILITY_UNKNOWN), and a host that reads a part
; reads such a document whole. One that changes nothing, a second id
; say, is read as the reader reads it, which is to ignore it. So is a
; channel after an item of an RSS feed's root, whose items the reader
; takes from the channel instead; a root the reader does not recognise
; is its own refusal, made at the root's start (`fail :invalid`). A
; document the grammar refuses fails the run after the events the passes
; before the refusal give, as the walk fails it. Over the 4,030
; documents of this repository's corpora (the rows of `test/spec/*.tsv`
; with the default options, `test/feedparser-wellformed/`, and the
; feedvalidator and feedparser trees `make fetch` fetches), read in Rust,
; TypeScript and Go, the part writes what the walk of the reader's value
; writes for every document the reader reads but two, each an element of
; the feed after its first entry (feedvalidator's
; `misplaced-metadata.xml` and `item_too_early.xml`), which it refuses,
; and fails where the reader fails for every other: the Rust and Go
; readers read 3,616 of them, and the TypeScript reader 13 more.
;
; The reading's state is [dialect stack]: the dialect once the root has
; begun, and a frame per open element, innermost last: [:root chan] for
; the root, whether an RSS feed's first channel has ended; [:channel] for
; that channel; [:node kids unit] for an element whose summary is written,
; what its child elements become and whether it is a unit; [:xh unit div]
; for an xhtml construct, whether its first div has begun; [:ser name
; opened first] for an element of its markup, whether its start tag's `>`
; is written and whether it is the first div; and [:skip] for an element
; the reader does not read. The writing's state is [:start], then [:head
; dialect els] while the members are held, `els` the members' units, and
; [:body dialect els] once they are written. Nothing grows with a
; document's length but the members held, under max_metadata_bytes.

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; Names
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------

; The namespace that makes a `feed` root Atom 0.3, not 1.0.
def feed-transduce-atom03 "http://purl.org/atom/ns#"

; The elements of a feed's own level the reader reads a member of the
; feed from, by dialect: Atom 1.0's and 0.3's children of the root; RSS's
; children of the channel, or of the root where there is no channel; and
; RSS 1.0's children of the root, its channel and its image (the
; channel's own children are read from inside it).
def feed-transduce-atom10-members ["id" "title" "updated" "author" "contributor" "category" "link" "generator" "icon" "logo" "rights" "subtitle"]

def feed-transduce-atom03-members ["id" "title" "modified" "author" "contributor" "category" "link" "generator" "icon" "logo" "copyright" "tagline"]

def feed-transduce-rss-members ["title" "link" "description" "copyright" "managingEditor" "webMaster" "pubDate" "lastBuildDate" "generator" "image" "category"]

def feed-transduce-rdf-members ["channel" "image"]

; The Atom elements the reader reads as a text construct or a content,
; whose value is the markup they hold where their type is xhtml.
def feed-transduce-constructs ["title" "subtitle" "rights" "copyright" "summary" "tagline" "content"]

def feed-transduce-among [names name]
  match (count (filter (fn [n] (equal n name)) names))
    case 0 false
    case _ true

; An element's local name: its name after the first colon, or the whole
; name where it has none.
def feed-transduce-local [name]
  let [parts (first-split ":" name)]
    match (count parts)
      case 1 name
      case _ (get-path (path 1) parts)

; The default namespace a root element declares: the last of its xmlns
; and xmlns: attributes, as xml's reader takes it; "" for none.
def feed-transduce-default-namespace [attrs]
  let [declared (filter (fn [k] (match k (case "xmlns" true) (case "xmlns:" true) (case _ false))) (keys attrs))]
    match (count declared)
      case 0 ""
      case _ (get (top declared) attrs)

; A root element's namespace, from its own attributes, since nothing is
; above it: its prefix's, or the default namespace for no prefix.
def feed-transduce-namespace [name attrs]
  let [parts (first-split ":" name)]
    match (count parts)
      case 1 (feed-transduce-default-namespace attrs)
      case _
        match (get-path (path 0) parts)
          case "" (feed-transduce-default-namespace attrs)
          case "xml" "http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace"
          case prefix (get-or (string-join "" ["xmlns:" prefix]) "" attrs)

; The dialect a root element names, as the reader detects it: Atom 0.3
; or 1.0 for a `feed`, RSS for an `rss`, RSS 1.0 for an `RDF`. Any other
; root is the reader's own refusal, made here before anything is written.
def feed-transduce-dialect [name local attrs]
  match local
    case "feed"
      match (feed-transduce-namespace name attrs)
        case feed-transduce-atom03 "atom03"
        case _ "atom10"
    case "rss" "rss"
    case "RDF" "rdf"
    case _ (fail :invalid (string-join "" ["feed: unrecognized root element \"" local "\"; expected one of feed, rss, RDF"]))

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; The reading: the rule passes in, the units out
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------

def feed-transduce-mark [frame stack]
  push frame (pop stack)

; The events that begin an element's summary: its local name, its
; attributes in order, and the list `c` of what it holds or `x` of the
; pieces of its markup.
def feed-transduce-begin [local attrs list]
  flatten
    vector
      [object-start (key "l") (scalar local) (key "a") object-start]
      flatten (map (fn [k] [(key k) (scalar (get k attrs))]) (keys attrs))
      [object-end (key list) array-start]

; An attribute's value as the reader serialises it: &, ", < and >
; escaped, in that order.
def feed-transduce-escape [value]
  string-join "&gt;" (split ">" (string-join "&lt;" (split "<" (string-join "&quot;" (split "\"" (string-join "&amp;" (split "&" value)))))))

; A serialised element's start tag, but for the `>` or `/>` that ends it.
def feed-transduce-start-tag [name attrs]
  string-join "" (push-all (map (fn [k] (string-join "" [" " k "=\"" (feed-transduce-escape (get k attrs)) "\""])) (keys attrs)) ["<" name])

; Whether an element is an Atom text construct or content of type xhtml.
def feed-transduce-xhtml [dialect local attrs]
  match dialect
    case "atom10" (if (feed-transduce-among feed-transduce-constructs local) (equal (get "type" attrs) "xhtml") false)
    case "atom03" (if (feed-transduce-among feed-transduce-constructs local) (equal (get "type" attrs) "xhtml") false)
    case _ false

def feed-transduce-skip [dialect stack]
  transition [dialect (push [:skip] stack)] []

; A member of the feed: a unit `m` of its own.
def feed-transduce-member [dialect stack local attrs]
  if (feed-transduce-xhtml dialect local attrs)
    transition [dialect (push [:xh true false] stack)] (push-all (feed-transduce-begin local attrs "x") [object-start (key "m")])
    transition [dialect (push [:node :leaf true] stack)] (push-all (feed-transduce-begin local attrs "c") [object-start (key "m")])

; An element of the feed's own level: an entry, a unit `e` of its own, a
; member of the feed, or nothing the reader reads.
def feed-transduce-unit [dialect stack members entry local attrs]
  if (equal local entry)
    transition [dialect (push [:node :sub true] stack)] (push-all (feed-transduce-begin local attrs "c") [object-start (key "e")])
    if (feed-transduce-among members local)
      feed-transduce-member dialect stack local attrs
      feed-transduce-skip dialect stack

; A child of the root: in RSS, the first channel, `ch`, after which
; nothing else of the root is read.
def feed-transduce-top [dialect stack chan local attrs]
  match dialect
    case "rss"
      match [chan local]
        case [:done _] (feed-transduce-skip dialect stack)
        case [_ "channel"] (transition [dialect (push [:channel] stack)] [object-start (key "ch") (scalar true) object-end])
        case _ (feed-transduce-unit dialect stack feed-transduce-rss-members "item" local attrs)
    case "rdf" (feed-transduce-unit dialect stack feed-transduce-rdf-members "item" local attrs)
    case "atom10" (feed-transduce-unit dialect stack feed-transduce-atom10-members "entry" local attrs)
    case "atom03" (feed-transduce-unit dialect stack feed-transduce-atom03-members "entry" local attrs)

; A child of an element whose summary is being written.
def feed-transduce-nested [dialect stack kids local attrs]
  match kids
    case :sub
      if (feed-transduce-xhtml dialect local attrs)
        transition [dialect (push [:xh false false] stack)] (feed-transduce-begin local attrs "x")
        transition [dialect (push [:node :leaf false] stack)] (feed-transduce-begin local attrs "c")
    case :leaf (transition [dialect (push [:node :skip false] stack)] (feed-transduce-begin local attrs "c"))
    case :skip (feed-transduce-skip dialect stack)

; Content begins in a serialised element: its start tag's `>`, once, and
; in the first div, the mark where its inner markup begins.
def feed-transduce-content [stack name opened first]
  if opened
    [stack []]
    [(feed-transduce-mark [:ser name true first] stack) (if first [(scalar ">") (scalar true)] [(scalar ">")])]

; A child element of an xhtml construct: the first div is marked.
def feed-transduce-xh-child [dialect stack unit div name local attrs]
  if (if div false (equal local "div"))
    transition [dialect (push [:ser name false true] (feed-transduce-mark [:xh unit true] stack))] [(scalar (feed-transduce-start-tag name attrs))]
    transition [dialect (push [:ser name false false] stack)] [(scalar (feed-transduce-start-tag name attrs))]

def feed-transduce-ser-child [dialect stack n opened first name attrs]
  match (feed-transduce-content stack n opened first)
    case [rest outputs] (transition [dialect (push [:ser name false false] rest)] (push (scalar (feed-transduce-start-tag name attrs)) outputs))

; An element's start.
def feed-transduce-element [dialect stack tag]
  let [name (get "name" tag) attrs (get "attributes" tag) local (feed-transduce-local name)]
    match (count stack)
      case 0
        let [found (feed-transduce-dialect name local attrs)]
          transition [found [[:root :none]]] [array-start object-start (key "start") (scalar found) object-end]
      case _
        match (top stack)
          case [:root chan] (feed-transduce-top dialect stack chan local attrs)
          case [:channel] (feed-transduce-unit dialect stack feed-transduce-rss-members "item" local attrs)
          case [:skip] (feed-transduce-skip dialect stack)
          case [:node kids unit] (feed-transduce-nested dialect stack kids local attrs)
          case [:xh unit div] (feed-transduce-xh-child dialect stack unit div name local attrs)
          case [:ser n opened first] (feed-transduce-ser-child dialect stack n opened first name attrs)

; A text: what an element whose summary is written holds, or a piece of
; the markup. An empty text changes neither.
def feed-transduce-text [state dialect stack text]
  match [text (count stack)]
    case ["" _] (transition state [])
    case [_ 0] (transition state [])
    case _
      match (top stack)
        case [:node kids unit] (transition state [(scalar text)])
        case [:xh unit div] (transition state [(scalar text)])
        case [:ser n opened first]
          match (feed-transduce-content stack n opened first)
            case [rest outputs] (transition [dialect rest] (push (scalar text) outputs))
        case _ (transition state [])

; An element's end.
def feed-transduce-end [dialect stack]
  match (count stack)
    case 0 (fail :protocol-order "an element closed with none open, which a document's never do")
    case _
      let [rest (pop stack)]
        match (top stack)
          case [:root chan] (transition [dialect rest] [array-end])
          case [:channel] (transition [dialect (feed-transduce-mark [:root :done] rest)] [])
          case [:skip] (transition [dialect rest] [])
          case [:node kids true] (transition [dialect rest] [array-end object-end object-end])
          case [:node kids false] (transition [dialect rest] [array-end object-end])
          case [:xh true div] (transition [dialect rest] [array-end object-end object-end])
          case [:xh false div] (transition [dialect rest] [array-end object-end])
          case [:ser n true true] (transition [dialect rest] [(scalar false) (scalar (string-join "" ["</" n ">"]))])
          case [:ser n true false] (transition [dialect rest] [(scalar (string-join "" ["</" n ">"]))])
          case [:ser n false true] (transition [dialect rest] [(scalar true) (scalar false) (scalar "/>")])
          case [:ser n false false] (transition [dialect rest] [(scalar "/>")])

def feed-transduce-read [state pass]
  match state
    case [dialect stack]
      match pass
        case (open rule)
          match (get :name rule)
            case "element"
              match (transduce-token 0 rule)
                case missing (transition state [])
                case token (feed-transduce-element dialect stack (get :val token))
            case "child"
              match (transduce-token 0 rule)
                case missing (transition state [])
                case token (feed-transduce-text state dialect stack (get :val token))
            case _ (transition state [])
        case (close rule)
          match (get :name rule)
            case "element" (feed-transduce-end dialect stack)
            case _ (transition state [])

def feed-transduce-read-finish [state]
  match state
    case ["" []] (fail :protocol-order "the rule passes ended with no root element, which a document's never do")
    case [dialect []] []
    case _ (fail :protocol-order "the rule passes ended inside an element, which a document's never do")

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; Values: what the reader makes of an element's summary
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------

; What an element holds, its texts and its elements in order.
def feed-transduce-holds [el]
  get-or "c" [] el

; Every element `els` holds whose local name is `name`, and the first.
def feed-transduce-all [name els]
  filter (fn [c] (match (kind c) (case :record (equal (get "l" c) name)) (case _ false))) els

def feed-transduce-find [name els]
  get-path (path 0) (feed-transduce-all name els)

; An element's own text, trimmed: the reader's textOf, "" for none.
def feed-transduce-text-of [el]
  trim (string-join "" (filter (fn [c] (match (kind c) (case :string true) (case _ false))) (feed-transduce-holds el)))

; An attribute's value, or missing; and the same, missing for "" too,
; the reader's `if (a.x)`.
def feed-transduce-attr [name el]
  get name (get-or "a" (record) el)

def feed-transduce-truthy [name el]
  match (feed-transduce-attr name el)
    case "" missing
    case value value

; A member, `name` and the events of its value; none for no events.
def feed-transduce-pair [name events]
  match events
    case [] []
    case _ (push-all events [(key name)])

; A member whose value is text: none for missing.
def feed-transduce-string [name value]
  match value
    case missing []
    case _ [(key name) (scalar value)]

; A member whose value is text the reader keeps only where it is not
; empty.
def feed-transduce-some [name value]
  match value
    case "" []
    case _ [(key name) (scalar value)]

; A list member, its items' events; none for no items.
def feed-transduce-list [name items]
  match items
    case [] []
    case _ (flatten [[(key name) array-start] (flatten items) [array-end]])

; A text construct of a type and a value.
def feed-transduce-typed [type value]
  [object-start (key "type") (scalar type) (key "value") (scalar value) object-end]

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; Numbers: parseInt(text, 10), as the reader reads a link's length
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------

def feed-transduce-digits [[48 57]]

; The text with each ASCII digit written as a zero.
def feed-transduce-zeros [text]
  string-join "0" (split "1" (string-join "0" (split "2" (string-join "0" (split "3" (string-join "0" (split "4" (string-join "0" (split "5" (string-join "0" (split "6" (string-join "0" (split "7" (string-join "0" (split "8" (string-join "0" (split "9" text)))))))))))))))))

def feed-transduce-nonempty [parts]
  get-path (path 0) (filter (fn [p] (match p (case "" false) (case _ true))) parts)

; The run of ASCII digits a text begins with, "" for none: with its
; digits as zeros, the text splits at them into what is not a digit, and
; the first such run that is not empty follows the digits it begins with.
def feed-transduce-run [text]
  if (chars-within feed-transduce-digits text)
    text
    get-path (path 0) (first-split (feed-transduce-nonempty (split "0" (feed-transduce-zeros text))) text)

; A run of digits without the zeros it begins with, "0" for zeros alone.
def feed-transduce-unpad [run]
  if (chars-within [[48 48]] run)
    "0"
    let [lead (feed-transduce-nonempty (split "0" run))]
      string-join "" [lead (get-path (path 1) (first-split lead run))]

def feed-transduce-signed [sign text]
  match (feed-transduce-run text)
    case "" (number "NaN")
    case run (number (string-join "" [sign (feed-transduce-unpad run)]))

; parseInt(text, 10): white space skipped, a sign, and the longest run of
; ASCII digits after it, as a number; NaN where there is no digit.
def feed-transduce-int [text]
  let [t (trim text)]
    if (starts-with "-" t)
      feed-transduce-signed "-" (get-path (path 1) (first-split "-" t))
      if (starts-with "+" t)
        feed-transduce-signed "" (get-path (path 1) (first-split "+" t))
        feed-transduce-signed "" t

; A link's length: the number parseInt reads, or, where the feed's
; members are compared (`exact` false), the text it is read from, since
; NaN equals nothing.
def feed-transduce-length [exact el]
  match (feed-transduce-truthy "length" el)
    case missing []
    case text (if exact [(key "length") (scalar (feed-transduce-int text))] [(key "length") (scalar text)])

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; Atom 1.0 and 0.3
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------

; An xhtml construct's markup, as the reader serialises it: the inner
; markup of its first div, between the two marks, where it has one, and
; all of it otherwise.
def feed-transduce-pieces [x is]
  string-join "" (filter (fn [p] (match (kind p) (case :string true) (case _ false))) (map (fn [i] (get-path (path i) x)) is))

def feed-transduce-markup [el]
  let [x (get-or "x" [] el) marks (filter (fn [i] (match (kind (get-path (path i) x)) (case :boolean true) (case _ false))) (indices x))]
    match marks
      case [] (feed-transduce-pieces x (indices x))
      case [b e] (feed-transduce-pieces x (filter (fn [i] (match [(compare i b) (compare i e)] (case [:greater :less] true) (case _ false))) (indices x)))
      case _ (fail :protocol-order "an xhtml construct holds more than one first div")

; A text construct, the reader's parseText: its type, text where the
; attribute names none, and its value, its text or its markup.
def feed-transduce-type [el]
  match (feed-transduce-truthy "type" el)
    case missing "text"
    case type type

def feed-transduce-value [type el]
  match type
    case "xhtml" (feed-transduce-markup el)
    case _ (feed-transduce-text-of el)

def feed-transduce-construct [name el]
  match el
    case missing []
    case _
      let [type (feed-transduce-type el)]
        feed-transduce-pair name (feed-transduce-typed type (feed-transduce-value type el))

; A content, the reader's parseContent: its type, its src where it has
; one, and its value.
def feed-transduce-content-of [el]
  match el
    case missing []
    case _
      let [type (feed-transduce-type el)]
        flatten
          vector
            [(key "content") object-start (key "type") (scalar type)]
            feed-transduce-string "src" (feed-transduce-truthy "src" el)
            [(key "value") (scalar (feed-transduce-value type el)) object-end]

; A member whose value is an element's text, where the element is.
def feed-transduce-element-text [name el]
  match el
    case missing []
    case _ [(key name) (scalar (feed-transduce-text-of el))]

; A person, the reader's parsePerson: its name's text, its uri (or url)
; and its email where they have text.
def feed-transduce-person [el]
  let [holds (feed-transduce-holds el)
       uri (feed-transduce-text-of (feed-transduce-find "uri" holds))
       url (feed-transduce-text-of (feed-transduce-find "url" holds))]
    flatten
      vector
        [object-start (key "name") (scalar (feed-transduce-text-of (feed-transduce-find "name" holds)))]
        feed-transduce-some "uri" (match uri (case "" url) (case _ uri))
        feed-transduce-some "email" (feed-transduce-text-of (feed-transduce-find "email" holds))
        [object-end]

; A link, the reader's parseLink.
def feed-transduce-link [exact el]
  flatten
    vector
      [object-start (key "href") (scalar (match (feed-transduce-attr "href" el) (case missing "") (case href href)))]
      feed-transduce-string "rel" (feed-transduce-truthy "rel" el)
      feed-transduce-string "type" (feed-transduce-truthy "type" el)
      feed-transduce-string "hreflang" (feed-transduce-truthy "hreflang" el)
      feed-transduce-string "title" (feed-transduce-truthy "title" el)
      feed-transduce-length exact el
      [object-end]

; A category, the reader's parseCategory: its term, or its text, and its
; scheme and label where the attributes are, empty or not.
def feed-transduce-category [el]
  flatten
    vector
      [object-start (key "term") (scalar (match (feed-transduce-truthy "term" el) (case missing (feed-transduce-text-of el)) (case term term)))]
      feed-transduce-string "scheme" (feed-transduce-attr "scheme" el)
      feed-transduce-string "label" (feed-transduce-attr "label" el)
      [object-end]

; A generator, the reader's parseGenerator.
def feed-transduce-generator [el]
  match el
    case missing []
    case _
      flatten
        vector
          [(key "generator") object-start]
          feed-transduce-string "uri" (feed-transduce-attr "uri" el)
          feed-transduce-string "version" (feed-transduce-attr "version" el)
          [(key "value") (scalar (feed-transduce-text-of el)) object-end]

; The members of an Atom feed but its format, version and entries, from
; the elements of its own level held so far.
def feed-transduce-atom-head [atom03 exact els]
  flatten
    vector
      feed-transduce-element-text "id" (feed-transduce-find "id" els)
      feed-transduce-construct "title" (feed-transduce-find "title" els)
      feed-transduce-element-text "updated" (feed-transduce-find (if atom03 "modified" "updated") els)
      feed-transduce-list "authors" (map feed-transduce-person (feed-transduce-all "author" els))
      feed-transduce-list "contributors" (map feed-transduce-person (feed-transduce-all "contributor" els))
      feed-transduce-list "categories" (map feed-transduce-category (feed-transduce-all "category" els))
      feed-transduce-list "links" (map (partial feed-transduce-link exact) (feed-transduce-all "link" els))
      feed-transduce-generator (feed-transduce-find "generator" els)
      feed-transduce-element-text "icon" (feed-transduce-find "icon" els)
      feed-transduce-element-text "logo" (feed-transduce-find "logo" els)
      feed-transduce-construct "rights" (feed-transduce-find (if atom03 "copyright" "rights") els)
      feed-transduce-construct "subtitle" (feed-transduce-find (if atom03 "tagline" "subtitle") els)

; An Atom entry, the reader's parseAtomEntry.
def feed-transduce-atom-entry [atom03 el]
  let [els (feed-transduce-holds el)]
    flatten
      vector
        [object-start]
        feed-transduce-element-text "id" (feed-transduce-find "id" els)
        feed-transduce-construct "title" (feed-transduce-find "title" els)
        feed-transduce-element-text "updated" (feed-transduce-find (if atom03 "modified" "updated") els)
        feed-transduce-element-text "published" (feed-transduce-find (if atom03 "issued" "published") els)
        feed-transduce-list "authors" (map feed-transduce-person (feed-transduce-all "author" els))
        feed-transduce-list "contributors" (map feed-transduce-person (feed-transduce-all "contributor" els))
        feed-transduce-list "categories" (map feed-transduce-category (feed-transduce-all "category" els))
        feed-transduce-list "links" (map (partial feed-transduce-link true) (feed-transduce-all "link" els))
        feed-transduce-content-of (feed-transduce-find "content" els)
        feed-transduce-construct "rights" (feed-transduce-find (if atom03 "copyright" "rights") els)
        feed-transduce-construct "summary" (feed-transduce-find (if atom03 "tagline" "summary") els)
        [object-end]

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; RSS: an author, managingEditor or webMaster as an Atom person
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------

; The white space of JavaScript's \s, which `trim` takes off too.
def feed-transduce-spaces ["\t" "\n" "\u000b" "\u000c" "\r" " " " " " " " " " " " " " " " " " " " " " " " " " " " " " " " " " " " " "　" "﻿"]

; The text up to its first white space: each white space character cuts
; a prefix of the text, and the shortest prefix sorts first.
def feed-transduce-word [text]
  get-path (path 0) (sort (map (fn [c] (get-path (path 0) (first-split c text))) feed-transduce-spaces))

; The text through the first @ after its first character, within its
; part before any white space or parenthesis: the shortest X@ the
; pattern's [^\s()]+@ matches; missing where there is none.
def feed-transduce-at [word]
  let [parts (split "@" (get-path (path 0) (first-split "(" (get-path (path 0) (first-split ")" word)))))]
    match [(count parts) (get-path (path 0) parts)]
      case [1 _] missing
      case [2 ""] missing
      case [_ ""] (string-join "" ["@" (get-path (path 1) parts) "@"])
      case [_ x] (string-join "" [x "@"])

; Whether a is longer than b.
def feed-transduce-longer [a b]
  match (compare (length a) (length b))
    case :greater true
    case _ false

; The name of `(name)`, the rest of the text after an address: missing
; unless it opens with ( and its one ) ends it, with something between.
def feed-transduce-parenthesised [rest]
  if (starts-with "(" rest)
    feed-transduce-closing (get-path (path 1) (first-split "(" rest))
    missing

; The name before a closing ) that is the text's only one and its last
; character, where it is not empty.
def feed-transduce-closing [inner]
  let [parts (split ")" inner)]
    match parts
      case [name ""] (match name (case "" missing) (case _ name))
      case _ missing

; An RSS person, the reader's parseRssPerson: its text matched against
; /^\s*([^\s()]+@\S+)\s*(?:\(([^)]+)\))?\s*$/ as JavaScript's engine
; matches it, the address its email and the name in parentheses its name
; (the address where there is none), and the text its name where the
; pattern does not match. The text is trimmed, so an address is its first
; word, or, where that word holds a ( after the address's first character
; past its @, its part before the last such (.
def feed-transduce-rss-person [text]
  let [word (feed-transduce-word text) at (feed-transduce-at word)]
    match at
      case missing (feed-transduce-named text missing)
      case _
        if (equal word text)
          if (feed-transduce-longer text at)
            feed-transduce-named text text
            feed-transduce-named text missing
          feed-transduce-spaced text word at

; A text holding white space: the address its first word, followed by
; white space and a parenthesised name; or the first word's part before
; its last (, the rest of the text from there the parenthesised name.
def feed-transduce-spaced [text word at]
  let [rest (get-path (path 1) (first-split word text))
       whole (if (feed-transduce-longer word at) (feed-transduce-parenthesised (trim rest)) missing)]
    match whole
      case missing (feed-transduce-cut text word at rest)
      case name (feed-transduce-named name word)

def feed-transduce-cut [text word at rest]
  let [parts (split "(" word)]
    match (count parts)
      case 1 (feed-transduce-named text missing)
      case _
        let [address (string-join "(" (pop parts))]
          if (feed-transduce-longer address at)
            match (feed-transduce-closing (string-join "" [(top parts) rest]))
              case missing (feed-transduce-named text missing)
              case name (feed-transduce-named name address)
            feed-transduce-named text missing

; A person of a name and, where there is one, an email.
def feed-transduce-named [name email]
  match email
    case missing [object-start (key "name") (scalar name) object-end]
    case _ [object-start (key "name") (scalar name) (key "email") (scalar email) object-end]

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; RSS 2.0, 0.92 and 0.91, as the reader maps them onto Atom
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------

; A text construct of type text, where its value is not empty.
def feed-transduce-rss-text [name value]
  match value
    case "" []
    case _ (push-all (feed-transduce-typed "text" value) [(key name)])

; A link of an href and a rel, where the href is not empty.
def feed-transduce-rel [href rel]
  match href
    case "" []
    case _ [[object-start (key "href") (scalar href) (key "rel") (scalar rel) object-end]]

; An RSS category as an Atom one: its text the term, its domain, where
; the attribute is, the scheme.
def feed-transduce-rss-category [el]
  flatten
    vector
      [object-start (key "term") (scalar (feed-transduce-text-of el))]
      feed-transduce-string "scheme" (feed-transduce-attr "domain" el)
      [object-end]

; A list of one person, where the text is not empty.
def feed-transduce-rss-people [text]
  match text
    case "" []
    case _ (flatten [[(key "authors") array-start] (feed-transduce-rss-person text) [array-end]])

; The members of the feed an RSS channel maps onto, from the elements of
; its own level held so far: the channel's, or the root's where the root
; has no channel.
def feed-transduce-rss-head [els]
  let [link (feed-transduce-text-of (feed-transduce-find "link" els))
       built (feed-transduce-text-of (feed-transduce-find "lastBuildDate" els))
       generator (feed-transduce-text-of (feed-transduce-find "generator" els))
       editor (feed-transduce-text-of (feed-transduce-find "managingEditor" els))]
    flatten
      vector
        feed-transduce-rss-text "title" (feed-transduce-text-of (feed-transduce-find "title" els))
        feed-transduce-rss-text "subtitle" (feed-transduce-text-of (feed-transduce-find "description" els))
        feed-transduce-rss-text "rights" (feed-transduce-text-of (feed-transduce-find "copyright" els))
        feed-transduce-some "id" link
        feed-transduce-some "updated" (match built (case "" (feed-transduce-text-of (feed-transduce-find "pubDate" els))) (case _ built))
        match generator
          case "" []
          case _ [(key "generator") object-start (key "value") (scalar generator) object-end]
        feed-transduce-some "logo" (feed-transduce-text-of (feed-transduce-find "url" (feed-transduce-holds (feed-transduce-find "image" els))))
        feed-transduce-list "links" (feed-transduce-rel link "alternate")
        feed-transduce-list "categories" (map feed-transduce-rss-category (feed-transduce-all "category" els))
        feed-transduce-rss-people (match editor (case "" (feed-transduce-text-of (feed-transduce-find "webMaster" els))) (case _ editor))

; An item's enclosure as a link, where it has a url.
def feed-transduce-enclosure [el]
  match (feed-transduce-truthy "url" el)
    case missing []
    case url
      vector
        flatten
          vector
            [object-start (key "href") (scalar url) (key "rel") (scalar "enclosure")]
            feed-transduce-string "type" (feed-transduce-truthy "type" el)
            feed-transduce-length true el
            [object-end]

; An item's comments as a link, where they have text.
def feed-transduce-replies [comments]
  match comments
    case "" []
    case _ [[object-start (key "href") (scalar comments) (key "rel") (scalar "replies") (key "type") (scalar "text/html") object-end]]

; An item's source as an Atom source.
def feed-transduce-source [el]
  match el
    case missing []
    case _
      flatten
        vector
          [(key "source") object-start (key "format") (scalar "atom") (key "version") (scalar "1.0")]
          feed-transduce-rss-text "title" (feed-transduce-text-of el)
          match (feed-transduce-truthy "url" el)
            case missing []
            case url (feed-transduce-list "links" (feed-transduce-rel url "self"))
          [object-end]

; An RSS item as an Atom entry, the reader's rss2ItemToAtomEntry.
def feed-transduce-rss-entry [el]
  let [els (feed-transduce-holds el)
       link (feed-transduce-text-of (feed-transduce-find "link" els))
       description (feed-transduce-text-of (feed-transduce-find "description" els))
       published (feed-transduce-text-of (feed-transduce-find "pubDate" els))
       guid (feed-transduce-find "guid" els)]
    flatten
      vector
        [object-start]
        feed-transduce-rss-text "title" (feed-transduce-text-of (feed-transduce-find "title" els))
        match description
          case "" []
          case _ (push-all (feed-transduce-typed "html" description) [(key "summary")])
        match published
          case "" []
          case _ [(key "published") (scalar published) (key "updated") (scalar published)]
        match guid
          case missing (feed-transduce-some "id" link)
          case _ [(key "id") (scalar (feed-transduce-text-of guid))]
        feed-transduce-list "links" (flatten [(feed-transduce-rel link "alternate") (feed-transduce-enclosure (feed-transduce-find "enclosure" els)) (feed-transduce-replies (feed-transduce-text-of (feed-transduce-find "comments" els)))])
        feed-transduce-rss-people (feed-transduce-text-of (feed-transduce-find "author" els))
        feed-transduce-list "categories" (map feed-transduce-rss-category (feed-transduce-all "category" els))
        feed-transduce-source (feed-transduce-find "source" els)
        [object-end]

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; RSS 1.0 and 0.90, as the reader maps them onto Atom
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------

; The members of the feed an RSS 1.0 document maps onto, from its first
; channel and its first image.
def feed-transduce-rdf-head [els]
  let [channel (feed-transduce-find "channel" els)
       holds (feed-transduce-holds channel)
       link (feed-transduce-text-of (feed-transduce-find "link" holds))
       about (match (feed-transduce-truthy "rdf:about" channel) (case missing "") (case about about))]
    flatten
      vector
        feed-transduce-rss-text "title" (feed-transduce-text-of (feed-transduce-find "title" holds))
        feed-transduce-rss-text "subtitle" (feed-transduce-text-of (feed-transduce-find "description" holds))
        feed-transduce-some "id" (match about (case "" link) (case _ about))
        feed-transduce-list "links" (feed-transduce-rel link "alternate")
        feed-transduce-some "logo" (feed-transduce-text-of (feed-transduce-find "url" (feed-transduce-holds (feed-transduce-find "image" els))))

; An RSS 1.0 item as an Atom entry: its id its rdf:about, or its link.
def feed-transduce-rdf-entry [el]
  let [els (feed-transduce-holds el)
       link (feed-transduce-text-of (feed-transduce-find "link" els))]
    flatten
      vector
        [object-start]
        feed-transduce-rss-text "title" (feed-transduce-text-of (feed-transduce-find "title" els))
        feed-transduce-rss-text "summary" (feed-transduce-text-of (feed-transduce-find "description" els))
        [(key "id") (scalar (match (feed-transduce-truthy "rdf:about" el) (case missing link) (case about about)))]
        feed-transduce-list "links" (feed-transduce-rel link "alternate")
        [object-end]

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; The writing: the units in, the feed's events out
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------

def feed-transduce-captures
  vector
    capture :start (path each-index "start") :max_metadata_bytes
    capture :channel (path each-index "ch") :max_metadata_bytes
    capture :member (path each-index "m") :max_metadata_bytes
    capture :entry (path each-index "e") :max_record_bytes

; The feed's members but its format, version and entries.
def feed-transduce-head [dialect exact els]
  match dialect
    case "atom10" (feed-transduce-atom-head false exact els)
    case "atom03" (feed-transduce-atom-head true exact els)
    case "rss" (feed-transduce-rss-head els)
    case "rdf" (feed-transduce-rdf-head els)

def feed-transduce-entry [dialect el]
  match dialect
    case "atom10" (feed-transduce-atom-entry false el)
    case "atom03" (feed-transduce-atom-entry true el)
    case "rss" (feed-transduce-rss-entry el)
    case "rdf" (feed-transduce-rdf-entry el)

; A member of the feed after its first entry: nothing, where the feed's
; members are what was written; refused otherwise.
def feed-transduce-late [dialect els el]
  let [more (push el els)]
    if (equal (feed-transduce-head dialect false els) (feed-transduce-head dialect false more))
      transition [:body dialect more] []
      fail :unstreamable (string-join "" ["a feed's " (get "l" el) " element after its first entry, which changes the feed's members, written before its entries"])

def feed-transduce-write [state item]
  match [state item]
    case [[:start] (selected :start dialect)] (transition [:head dialect []] [object-start (key "format") (scalar "atom") (key "version") (scalar (match dialect (case "atom03" "0.3") (case _ "1.0")))])
    case [[:head dialect els] (selected :member el)] (transition [:head dialect (push el els)] [])
    case [[:head dialect els] (selected :channel _)] (transition [:head dialect []] [])
    case [[:head dialect els] (selected :entry el)] (transition [:body dialect els] (flatten [(feed-transduce-head dialect true els) [(key "entries") array-start] (feed-transduce-entry dialect el)]))
    case [[:body dialect els] (selected :member el)] (feed-transduce-late dialect els el)
    case [[:body dialect els] (selected :channel _)] (fail :unstreamable "a channel after an item of the rss element, from which the reader reads the feed and its items in place of the rss element's")
    case [[:body dialect els] (selected :entry el)] (transition state (feed-transduce-entry dialect el))
    case _ (fail :protocol-order "the units of a feed came out of order, which the reading never makes")

def feed-transduce-done [state]
  match state
    case [:head dialect els] (flatten [(feed-transduce-head dialect true els) [(key "entries") array-start array-end object-end]])
    case [:body dialect els] [array-end object-end]
    case _ (fail :protocol-order "the units of a feed held no root element, which the reading never makes")

; The transducer: a feed's rule passes in, its tree's events out.
def feed-transduce [input]
  as-events
    scan-emit [:start] feed-transduce-write feed-transduce-done
      route feed-transduce-captures
        as-events (scan-emit ["" []] feed-transduce-read feed-transduce-read-finish (parser-events input))
